## Cave Serpent

Giant serpents live in a cavern deep below [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], in a wild cave where purple crystals on the ceiling cast a bluish glow and small creatures live in the pools. Algae grows in their water. They speak, and they keep watch on whoever enters their cavern.

They rise half out of the water to demand who a visitor is and whether they are allowed to be there. They ask to see a permission slip, and will try to eat it. Those they do not know, they judge not allowed, and attack.

At least four still live in the pools. Two others are dead.

## Chorister Bird

Chorister birds are flocks whose singing harmonizes into a hypnotic lure. They pull travellers off the path and toward other predators, which leave the remains for the birds to pick at.

## Glide Ape

Glide apes are a cross between a monkey and a flying squirrel: apes with flaps of skin in their arms that they use to glide from tree to tree. A pack of them lives in the canopy of the [[Verdant Expanse]] near where it is entered from [[Geography/Calaria/Wrenford|Wrenford]].

## Tallyhunt

Tallyhunts are the lean, wrong-jointed dog-things [[People/Galzu|Galzu]] summons. They move at right angles to the world, and their gaze pulls a body apart. They are hardest where the world is square: the hardness runs out of them near a curve in a structure, or away from a standing corner. They last only while their summoner holds them, and when Galzu fell at the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Tally|dead Heart]], hers faded where they stood.

## Vine Snake

Vine snakes climb the trunks of the [[Verdant Expanse]] disguised as ivy. The body carries scales that are barely visible, and it sprouts leaves as a plant would, so that only a careful look tells it apart from the vines around it.
